-- title:
--   Every selected persistent source region ends before the retained boundary
-- statement:
--   Let all layout addresses and sizes be natural numbers. Fix block parameters $h,J$, cutoff $c$, positive band size $g$, and source lengths $N_B,N_C$ at addresses $s_B,s_C$. Select valid band indices $i,j$ and an occurrence code $u<T^J$, where $T$ is the local schedule length. Let $p,b,f,o$ be the bases of the paired-band data, source bank, cover bundle, and occurrence rows. Assume both full source arrays, the paired-band allocation, the source-bank allocation, and the cover/key bundle end at or before $E$, and
--   $$o+T^J J\le b.$$
--   Let $X$ be the retained pointer record selected by $(i,j,u)$. Then
--   $$\operatorname{end}(R)\le E\quad\text{for every region }R\text{ in the selected-source contract}.$$
--   These regions are the pair, bank, and cover headers of lengths $3,5,16$; both six-cell band headers and single stage-pointer cells; both source slices, bucket-offset arrays, and flat index lists; the $J$-cell occurrence row; schedule maps, candidate indices, and two histograms; and both retained stage families of length $(512hJ+1)\sum_{v=0}^{\min(c,512hJ)}\binom{512hJ}{v}$.
--
--   The theorem supplies all address bounds needed to read this selected source configuration.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankResourceBoundsWantedAccess.lean#L72-L122

